WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.047
Now compare the agentic version.

00:00:02.047 --> 00:00:04.807
The workflow first routes the request.

00:00:04.807 --> 00:00:09.502
It recognizes that we need both policy search and order lookup.

00:00:09.502 --> 00:00:16.142
It retrieves the return policy, then obtains the order's delivery date from the structured system.

00:00:16.142 --> 00:00:20.524
After that, it checks whether the combined evidence is complete.

00:00:21.261 --> 00:00:27.798
If the policy is present and the order record is present, the system can generate a grounded answer.

00:00:27.798 --> 00:00:33.728
Then it validates citations and any important business constraints before stopping.

00:00:33.728 --> 00:00:38.913
This sequence is more reliable because each step has a clear purpose.

00:00:39.418 --> 00:00:42.950
Notice that the language model does not need to do everything.

00:00:42.950 --> 00:00:48.135
Retrieval finds documents. The database provides exact facts.

00:00:48.135 --> 00:00:50.785
Normal code can compare dates.

00:00:50.785 --> 00:00:55.985
The model can focus on interpreting language and composing a clear final answer.
